{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     post/docs-section — one documentation section: /docs/{section}/.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     bright's "folder". The post's body is the section overview; its documents
     are listed beneath it.

     ⚠ THE BRANCH THIS PARTIAL EXISTS FOR WAS MISSING, and the symptom is the
     one this project keeps meeting: /docs/platform-handbook/ rendered as a
     blog ARTICLE. #folders-col matched nothing in post.hbs, so a section fell
     through to {{else}}. It rendered, it was styled, and it was the wrong
     page — no error anywhere.

     ── COUNTED, NEVER TYPED ────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The document list is a {{#get}} over the collection, leaning on THE ONE
     RULE from routes.yaml: a section post's slug equals its own tag's slug,
     which is what makes /docs/{section}/ and /docs/{section}/{doc}/ line up.
     Break that and this quietly lists nothing.

     ⚠ limit is a NUMBER — Ghost's {{#get}} does not accept "all".

     .ns-tree rather than a card grid, for the reason in partials/docs/index.hbs:
     a reader in documentation is FINDING, not browsing.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<div class="ns-post ns-post--wide">
    <article class="ns-post__body">
        <header class="ns-posthead">
            <div class="ns-posthead__inner">
                <nav class="ns-breadcrumb" aria-label="{{t "Breadcrumb"}}">
                    <a href="{{@site.url}}/docs/">{{t "Docs"}}</a>
                </nav>
                <h1 class="ns-posthead__title">{{title}}</h1>
                {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-posthead__standfirst">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="gh-content ns-prose" id="post-body">{{content}}</div>

        {{#get "posts" filter="primary_tag:{{slug}}+tags:hash-docs-col" order="published_at asc" limit="100" as |docs|}}
            {{#if docs}}
                <ul class="ns-tree">
                    {{#foreach docs}}
                        <li><a class="ns-tree__node" href="{{url}}"><span class="ns-tree__label">{{title}}</span></a></li>
                    {{/foreach}}
                </ul>
            {{/if}}
        {{/get}}
    </article>
</div>
